---
// /privacy/ — We-Amp keeps one privacy notice for all its websites, this one
// included, at https://we-amp.com/privacy/. Production answers /privacy/ with a
// 301 to it from the server's redirect map; this page is what dev, preview and
// any server without that map serve, with its canonical on we-amp.com. The
// section on scan-result requests states what that form sends and how long the
// stored record is kept; keep it in step with the form in
// src/components/scan/ResultsView.astro and with the notice.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { VENDOR } from '../data/product-facts.mjs';

const NOTICE = 'https://we-amp.com/privacy/';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — mod_pagespeed"
  description={`${VENDOR} keeps one privacy notice for all its websites, modpagespeed.com included, at we-amp.com/privacy/.`}
  canonical={NOTICE}
>
  <PageHero title="Privacy" size="utility" width="prose">
    <Fragment slot="lede">
      {VENDOR} keeps one privacy notice for all its websites, modpagespeed.com included. It covers
      what this site and its tools do with personal data, how we handle support mail from
      subscribers, and what the software you install does and does not send. Read it at
      <a href={NOTICE} class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline">
        we-amp.com/privacy/
      </a>
      .
    </Fragment>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="container-prose pb-16">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Requests from a scan result</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
      When you send the form under a scan result, the request contains your email address, your note
      if you wrote one, the address of the page you scanned, the number of sites if you filled it
      in, the topics you ticked and the topics the scan flagged, and the findings of the scan for
      that page: its grade and score, its speed scores, the platform the scan detected, and the
      detail of the checks behind the topics you ticked.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
      The request is sent to {VENDOR} as an email and stored as a record in our database on Google
      Cloud. The record is kept for 24 months and then deleted automatically. The notice on
      we-amp.com says how long the copy in our mailbox and the application log are kept.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
